{
  "summary": "The proposed three-part fix is structurally sound but has two gaps worth addressing. First, the empty-sections guard (`if (newSections.length === 0) return;`) prevents legitimate empty-board states from ever rendering — if all features are genuinely removed or moved out of all stages, the board will be frozen showing stale cards indefinitely. A better guard would distinguish between 'server returned a plausible page with zero sections' versus 'response is too small or malformed to be a real board render' (e.g., check `html.indexOf('stage-section') === -1 && html.length < threshold`), or at minimum only suppress zero-section updates when the current board already has content. Second, moving the cache assignment after DOM update (fix 3) introduces a subtle redundant-work issue: if the server returns identical content on consecutive polls but the first poll triggered a full DOM replace (via the length-mismatch branch), the cache won't match on the next poll and the expensive DOM diffing will run again unnecessarily — the cache should still be updated even on early-return paths to prevent repeated re-processing of the same content."
}
